  "discussion": "Surf along north and west facing shores will build to warning levels today as a large, long-period north-northwest swell fills in. This swell will fade to advisory level heading into Wednesday before becoming overshadowed by an extra large, long-period north-northwest swell Wednesday night into Thursday that is expected to bring another round of warning level surf to north-and west-facing shores before gradually fading into the weekend. Surf heights along east-facing shores will increase today as north swell wraps into east shores. Due to the swell angle (350 degrees), eastern shores of Oahu have been included in the current High Surf Warning. Another round of wrapping swell is possible with the extra large north-northwest swell on Thursday into Friday. This swell will shift more northerly with time, so more swell energy will make it into east-facing shores by Friday even as the swell begins fading. Surf along south-facing shores will remain small through the period, with minor bumps in long-period energy expected late Wednesday and over the weekend.",
